      "message": "When you commit in this repo, you normally use a hook to insert `Change-Id: \u003cid\u003e` into your commit message. You have likely followed at some point an instruction to set it up using the following command:\n```\nf\u003d`git rev-parse --git-dir`/hooks/commit-msg ; mkdir -p $(dirname $f) ; curl -Lo $f https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/tools/hooks/commit-msg ; chmod +x $f\n```\nNow that I86db79d9065d626a9ea8516f46eea576a45b6067 introduced `.githooks/` and put a hook there, we need to make sure other hooks are also installed there, including the on-commit hook. To that end, I have run the following command locally and committed its result:\n```\nf\u003d\".githooks/commit-msg\" ; curl -Lo $f https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/tools/hooks/commit-msg ; chmod +x $f\n```",
